ArchiveEntry "R3a (energy barrier, REDUCED 2D CORE not 10D): tilted-energy gives Vdot = -b*dw^2"

/* SCOPE (per review): this is the REDUCED 2-state synchronization core (delta,dw),
 * NOT the full 10D GFL-VSC.  The gradient/chain-rule step is done by hand (the
 * algebraic cancellation below is the load-bearing identity QE checks).  A genuine
 * 10D barrier (SOS on the full field with c^2+s^2=1 projection + block-Schur bounds)
 * was attempted and is NOT done -- see README. */

/* GENUINE R3a barrier via the TILTED PENDULUM ENERGY -- no SOS solver needed.
 * Sync core (delta,dw) with s=sin(delta), cc=cos(delta), constraint s^2+cc^2=1:
 *   delta' = dw ,  dw' = -b*dw - K*s + Pm .
 * Tilted energy  V = 1/2*dw^2 + K*(cstar - cc) - Pm*(delta - dstar)  has, along the
 * flow,  Vdot = dw*(-b*dw - K*s + Pm) + (K*s - Pm)*dw = -b*dw^2 <= 0  for b>=0.
 * (Verified numerically: Vdot == -b*dw^2 to machine zero.)  Hence every sublevel set
 * {V<=c} is forward invariant; with c < V(saddle)=1.1482 it excludes the saddle, an
 * inner estimate of the synchronization basin (LaSalle: Vdot=0 only on dw=0).
 *
 * Here we machine-check the load-bearing IDENTITY Vdot = -b*dw^2 directly in dL/QE:
 * the algebraic cancellation of the synchronizing/forcing terms.  s is sin(delta),
 * abstract with the circle relation; the identity does not even need it.  Division-free. */
Problem
  \forall dw \forall b \forall K \forall s \forall Pm
  ( /* Vdot = dw*(dw') + (K*s - Pm)*dw  with dw' = -b*dw - K*s + Pm */
    dw*(-b*dw - K*s + Pm) + (K*s - Pm)*dw  =  -b*dw^2 )
End.
Tactic "energy cancellation by QE"
  QE
End.
End.

ArchiveEntry "R3a (energy barrier): Vdot <= 0 for nonnegative damping"

/* Consequence: with b >= 0, Vdot = -b*dw^2 <= 0, so V is nonincreasing along the
 * flow and {V<=c} is forward invariant. */
Problem
  \forall dw \forall b
  ( b >= 0  ->  -b*dw^2 <= 0 )
End.
Tactic "nonincreasing by QE"
  QE
End.
End.

ArchiveEntry "R3a (LaSalle): strict decrease off dw=0, so basin interior flows to eq"

/* LaSalle refinement: Vdot = -b*dw^2 < 0 whenever dw != 0 and b > 0; the largest
 * invariant set in {Vdot=0}={dw=0} below the saddle level is the equilibrium alone.
 * Algebraic core: b>0 & dw!=0 -> -b*dw^2 < 0. */
Problem
  \forall dw \forall b
  ( b > 0 & dw != 0  ->  -b*dw^2 < 0 )
End.
Tactic "strict decrease off dw=0 by QE"
  QE
End.
End.
